WT({ id: 'vpc-three-tier', title: 'VPC with public, private and isolated subnets across three zones', summary: 'A reusable network layout with a CIDR plan that leaves room to grow.',
  tasks: { saa: ['1.2', '3.4', '2.2'], sap: ['1.4'] },
  diagram: DG_VPC,
  intro: '<p>Use a /16 for the VPC and give each tier a /20 per zone. That is 4,091 usable addresses per subnet, with more than half the VPC left unallocated.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Zone a</th><th>Zone b</th><th>Zone c</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Public</th><td>10.20.0.0/20</td><td>10.20.16.0/20</td><td>10.20.32.0/20</td></tr><tr><th>Private</th><td>10.20.48.0/20</td><td>10.20.64.0/20</td><td>10.20.80.0/20</td></tr><tr><th>Isolated</th><td>10.20.96.0/20</td><td>10.20.112.0/20</td><td>10.20.128.0/20</td></tr><tr><th>Spare</th><td colspan="3">10.20.144.0/20 to 10.20.240.0/20</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Check the plan in the <a href="#tools/cidr">CIDR calculator</a>.</p>',
  flow: ['Inbound requests reach the load balancer in the public subnets through the internet gateway.', 'The load balancer forwards to application tasks in the private subnets.', 'Application tasks reach the database in the isolated subnets.', 'Outbound calls from private subnets leave through the NAT gateway in the same zone.', 'Calls to S3 and DynamoDB use gateway endpoints; isolated subnets reach other AWS services through interface endpoints.'],
  components: [['Internet gateway', 'Two-way internet path for public subnets'], ['NAT gateway (one per zone)', 'Outbound-only internet for private subnets'], ['Route tables', 'One public, one private per zone, one isolated'], ['Gateway and interface endpoints', 'Private paths to AWS services'], ['Flow logs', 'Record accepted and rejected traffic']],
  security: ['Only load balancers and NAT gateways live in public subnets.', 'Isolated subnets have no default route at all.', 'Security groups reference each other tier to tier.', 'Choose a CIDR that does not overlap any other VPC or on-premises range.'],
  cost: ['NAT gateways are the main fixed cost: three zones means three hourly charges plus per-GB processing.', 'Gateway endpoints are free and remove S3 traffic from NAT.', 'Non-production can use one NAT gateway and accept the availability risk.'],
  failures: [['One zone fails', 'Other zones keep their own NAT gateway and subnets; capacity must be sized for it'], ['Subnet runs out of addresses', 'Add a new subnet from spare space; subnets cannot be resized'], ['CIDR overlaps another network', 'Peering and Transit Gateway routing fail; fix needs a rebuild or PrivateLink']],
  related: [['service/vpc', 'Amazon VPC'], ['compare/subnet-types', 'Public vs private vs isolated subnets'], ['tools/cidr', 'CIDR calculator']] });

